# tools/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint_witness.rish -- the guard that names a repair can now make it.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint_witness.rish
#
# A shelf sits one directory below the pin it was folded out of, so every climbing link must gain a
# level. NOTHING WRITES THESE SHELVES -- a hand writes each one -- so every hand must remember, and in
# the week to `20260907` four different hands did not. A lantern that fires twice becomes a loom.
#
# The repair was never the hard part. `fold_shelf_link_scan.sh list` already prints the corrected
# path for every lost link, and it proposes one only after confirming that path EXISTS on disk. The
# answer was computed and a human was retyping it.
#
# THE SCAN STAYS THE AUTHORITY. This tool invents nothing: it applies the scan's `repair` column and
# nothing else, leaves a DEAD link alone because a broken link with no computed repair needs a
# reader, and writes through the original inode so a tracked file keeps its mode.
#
# AND IT READS THE WORKING TREE, WHERE THE GATE READS THE INDEX. The scan's corpus is `tracked` by
# default, because gating an untracked draft would refuse a hand mid-fold; this tool asks it for
# `working`, because the file needing the correction is exactly the one a hand has just written and
# has yet to stage. That difference is why the tree's own written remedy was inert: `20260908.044602`
# said run the repointer BEFORE staging, `20260908.063650` did precisely that, read
# `nothing_to_do`, and repaired nine links by hand -- one `git add` being the whole distance between
# the two answers. A prescription that cannot fire prescribes nothing. `--tracked-only` restores the
# elder population, an IGNORED path is refused under either, and the control proves all three.

say "fold-shelf-repoint: Language EN -- the fourth firing of one fault, answered once."
say "fold-shelf-repoint: Style Gauge, Meter -- the repair is applied, never guessed."
say "fold-shelf-repoint: Lens TAME -- safety first; every refusal proven from both sides."

say "fold-shelf-repoint: the control -- twenty behaviors on a real fold in a throwaway repository..."
let ctl = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint_control.sh"]
assert ctl.ok else "fold-shelf-repoint: the control refused --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"
assert ctl.out contains "pass=20 fail=0" else "fold-shelf-repoint: the control did not prove twenty behaviors --\n${ctl.out}\n${ctl.err}"

say "fold-shelf-repoint: and this tree reads clean, so the tool has nothing to do here..."
let dry = run ["sh" "tools/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh"]
assert dry.ok else "fold-shelf-repoint: the dry run refused --\n${dry.out}"
# invariant: a dry run NEVER writes, so the standing guard must still read clean after it.
let after = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/f/fold_shelf_link_scan.sh"]
assert after.out contains "verdict=ok" else "fold-shelf-repoint: the tree carries depth-lost links -- run the repointer with --apply"

say "GREEN: fold-shelf-repoint -- the scan computes the repair, the tool applies exactly that, and a dead link is left for a reader."
